1
00:00:00,560 --> 00:00:02,655
Every electric train is a chain.

2
00:00:02,655 --> 00:00:03,627
Pull it apart,

3
00:00:03,627 --> 00:00:05,838
and you can see every link.

4
00:00:06,160 --> 00:00:07,822
Up top, the catenary.

5
00:00:07,822 --> 00:00:10,222
Between New Haven and Boston,

6
00:00:10,222 --> 00:00:12,640
it carries 25,000 volts.

7
00:00:12,660 --> 00:00:14,349
A spring-loaded pantograph

8
00:00:14,349 --> 00:00:15,903
presses against the wire

9
00:00:15,903 --> 00:00:17,947
and pulls that power down.

10
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:19,493
Inside, a transformer

11
00:00:19,493 --> 00:00:20,425
steps it down,

12
00:00:20,425 --> 00:00:22,073
and a traction converter

13
00:00:22,073 --> 00:00:24,240
reshapes it for the motors.

14
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:25,774
The motors drive the axles

15
00:00:25,774 --> 00:00:27,147
through gears.

16
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:28,991
Now the clever part.

17
00:00:28,991 --> 00:00:30,360
The wheels aren't flat.

18
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:31,739
They're cones.

19
00:00:31,860 --> 00:00:32,612
On a curve,

20
00:00:32,612 --> 00:00:34,568
the wheelset slides outward,

21
00:00:34,568 --> 00:00:36,222
so the outer wheel rolls

22
00:00:36,222 --> 00:00:37,651
on a bigger diameter.

23
00:00:37,651 --> 00:00:39,796
The train steers itself.

24
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:41,127
And when it brakes,

25
00:00:41,127 --> 00:00:42,981
the motors become generators,

26
00:00:42,981 --> 00:00:44,776
sending energy back.

27
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:46,278
Above all of it:

28
00:00:46,278 --> 00:00:48,034
positive train control.

29
00:00:48,034 --> 00:00:48,833
GPS, radio,

30
00:00:48,833 --> 00:00:50,509
and onboard computers

31
00:00:50,509 --> 00:00:52,186
that can stop the train

32
00:00:52,186 --> 00:00:53,634
on their own.

33
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:56,296
Required by law since 2008.

34
00:00:56,296 --> 00:00:58,937
Live on every mandated line

35
00:00:58,937 --> 00:01:01,117
by the end of 2020.

36
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:02,807
Wire. Wheel. Signal.

37
00:01:02,807 --> 00:01:04,250
That's a train.
